# Canada: the days on which Lynx, the Canadian-dollar large-value payment system (real-time gross settlement, RTGS)
# run by Payments Canada, is closed. Lynx closes on the federal statutory holidays; when such a holiday falls on a
# Saturday or Sunday, the system closes on the next business day instead.
#
# Translated from holidays-events rules/catalog/ca.yaml.
#
# How to read a rule: "rule <key> for <event> in <scope> [valid from A] = <dates> with kind = ..., cites ...;".
# The part after "=" is a date expression evaluated for every year: "1 JUL" is the first of July, "1 MON SEP" the
# first Monday in September, "2 MON OCT" the second Monday in October, "EASTER - 2D" two days before Western Easter
# Sunday. "{SAT + 2D, SUN + 1D}" after a date moves it when it falls on a Saturday (two days forward, to Monday) or a
# Sunday (one day forward, to Monday); a weekday not named there leaves the date where it is. "> PREV MON" moves to
# the last Monday strictly before the date. The kind says what the day does: "closed" means Lynx does not settle
# payments on that day. Dates are inclusive. The full syntax is in README.md in this directory.
#
# Weekends: Lynx has the weekend Saturday and Sunday (see weekends.rules).
#
# Scopes used in this file:
#   central_bank:BOC        Bank of Canada; only an announced event, no rule.
#   settlement_system:LYNX  Lynx (CAD RTGS, Payments Canada): the settlement system for large Canadian-dollar
#                           payments, operated by Payments Canada; part of Canada (country:CA); time zone
#                           America/Toronto.
#
# Background (from the catalog's comments): Payments Canada publishes a "system closure schedule" that covers two
# years at a time (read in November 2026: 2026 and 2027). For example Boxing Day 2026 falls on a Saturday, so Lynx
# closes on Monday 28 December 2026; in 2027 Christmas Day falls on a Saturday, so Lynx closes on Monday 27 December
# (Christmas) and Tuesday 28 December (Boxing Day). These rules project the closures for the years beyond the
# published schedule; once Payments Canada publishes a year, its published closures take precedence over the rules.
# An archived 2023 schedule (Internet Archive) confirms that every weekend holiday closes the next business day.
# Only federal holidays are included: provincial holidays such as Ontario's Family Day or the Civic Holiday in
# August are NOT Lynx closures, unlike some Toronto business-day calendars used in financial software.

# =====================================================================================================================
# settlement_system:LYNX - Lynx, the Canadian-dollar RTGS of Payments Canada
# Who sets it: Payments Canada, in its system closure schedule (source payments_canada_closures); the underlying
# holidays are the federal statutory holidays of the Holidays Act and related federal laws.
# =====================================================================================================================

# New Year's Day, 1 January. Lynx is closed. If 1 January is a Saturday, Lynx closes on Monday 3 January instead;
# if it is a Sunday, on Monday 2 January.
# Legal basis: Payments Canada system closure schedule; Holidays Act.
rule lynx.new_years_day for new_years_day in settlement_system:LYNX = 1 JAN {SAT + 2D, SUN + 1D}
  with kind = closed
  cites "Payments Canada system closure schedule (Lynx, ACSS)" url "https://www.payments.ca/system-closure-schedule" label official;

# Good Friday: the Friday before Western Easter Sunday. Lynx is closed.
# Legal basis: Payments Canada system closure schedule.
rule lynx.good_friday for good_friday in settlement_system:LYNX = EASTER - 2D
  with kind = closed
  cites "Payments Canada system closure schedule (Lynx, ACSS)" url "https://www.payments.ca/system-closure-schedule" label official;

# Victoria Day: the Monday before 25 May, that is the last Monday strictly before 25 May (between 18 and 24 May).
# Lynx is closed.
# Legal basis: Payments Canada system closure schedule; Holidays Act section 2 ("the Monday immediately preceding
# the 25th day of May").
rule lynx.victoria_day for victoria_day in settlement_system:LYNX = 25 MAY > PREV MON
  with kind = closed
  cites "Payments Canada system closure schedule (Lynx, ACSS)" url "https://www.payments.ca/system-closure-schedule" label official;

# Canada Day, 1 July. Lynx is closed. If 1 July is a Saturday, Lynx closes on Monday 3 July instead; if it is a
# Sunday, on Monday 2 July.
# Legal basis: Payments Canada system closure schedule; Holidays Act section 2.
rule lynx.canada_day for canada_day in settlement_system:LYNX = 1 JUL {SAT + 2D, SUN + 1D}
  with kind = closed
  cites "Payments Canada system closure schedule (Lynx, ACSS)" url "https://www.payments.ca/system-closure-schedule" label official;

# Labour Day: the first Monday in September. Lynx is closed.
# Legal basis: Payments Canada system closure schedule.
rule lynx.labor_day for labor_day in settlement_system:LYNX = 1 MON SEP
  with kind = closed
  cites "Payments Canada system closure schedule (Lynx, ACSS)" url "https://www.payments.ca/system-closure-schedule" label official;

# National Day for Truth and Reconciliation, 30 September: a federal statutory holiday since 2021 (Statutes of
# Canada 2021, chapter 11), first observed on 30 September 2021. Lynx is closed. If 30 September is a Saturday,
# Lynx closes on Monday 2 October instead; if it is a Sunday, on Monday 1 October.
# Legal basis: Payments Canada system closure schedule; S.C. 2021, c. 11.
rule lynx.truth_and_reconciliation_day for truth_and_reconciliation_day in settlement_system:LYNX valid from 2021-09-30
  = 30 SEP {SAT + 2D, SUN + 1D}
  with kind = closed
  cites "Payments Canada system closure schedule (Lynx, ACSS)" url "https://www.payments.ca/system-closure-schedule" label official;

# Thanksgiving (Canada): the second Monday in October. Lynx is closed.
# Legal basis: Payments Canada system closure schedule.
rule lynx.thanksgiving_ca for thanksgiving_ca in settlement_system:LYNX = 2 MON OCT
  with kind = closed
  cites "Payments Canada system closure schedule (Lynx, ACSS)" url "https://www.payments.ca/system-closure-schedule" label official;

# Remembrance Day, 11 November. Lynx is closed. If 11 November is a Saturday, Lynx closes on Monday 13 November
# instead; if it is a Sunday, on Monday 12 November.
# Legal basis: Payments Canada system closure schedule.
rule lynx.remembrance_day for remembrance_day in settlement_system:LYNX = 11 NOV {SAT + 2D, SUN + 1D}
  with kind = closed
  cites "Payments Canada system closure schedule (Lynx, ACSS)" url "https://www.payments.ca/system-closure-schedule" label official;

# Christmas Day, 25 December. Lynx is closed. If 25 December is a Saturday, Lynx closes on Monday 27 December
# instead; if it is a Sunday, on Tuesday 27 December, because Monday 26 December is already closed for Boxing Day.
# Legal basis: Payments Canada system closure schedule.
rule lynx.christmas_day for christmas_day in settlement_system:LYNX = 25 DEC {SAT + 2D, SUN + 2D}
  with kind = closed
  cites "Payments Canada system closure schedule (Lynx, ACSS)" url "https://www.payments.ca/system-closure-schedule" label official;

# Boxing Day, 26 December. Lynx is closed. If 26 December is a Saturday, Lynx closes on Monday 28 December instead
# (as in 2026); if it is a Sunday, on Tuesday 28 December, because Christmas (then on Saturday 25) takes Monday 27
# (as in 2027).
# Legal basis: Payments Canada system closure schedule.
rule lynx.boxing_day for boxing_day in settlement_system:LYNX = 26 DEC {SAT + 2D, SUN + 2D}
  with kind = closed
  cites "Payments Canada system closure schedule (Lynx, ACSS)" url "https://www.payments.ca/system-closure-schedule" label official;

# =====================================================================================================================
# central_bank:BOC - Bank of Canada (the catalog keeps it in us.yaml, with the other North American rules)
# Who sets it: the Bank of Canada, in its schedule of policy rate announcements (source boc_rate_schedule).
# =====================================================================================================================

# Bank of Canada policy rate announcement: eight a year. Next year's dates come by press release in the summer; the
# policy rate page lists the current and the next year. No projection: no dates until announced.
# No rule: the dates are only announced (boc_rate_schedule); they are data for the evaluator, under the key
# boc.rate_announcement.
